"{\"edits\":[{\"start\":0,\"end\":1,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"For SFO–BKK on January 15, 2027, the Hong Kong Aeroplan award is a strong option if you want the shortest elapsed journey among these four awards: it arrives at 10:35 a.m. on January 17, earlier than the other late-arriving options. It is not the earliest arrival overall; the Taipei award arriving at 1:25 a.m. gets in 9h 10m earlier. Compare the reported points, taxes, seat counts, and schedules below; award quote scopes are unknown.\"}]},{\"start\":3,\"end\":4,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J7@2027-01-15T12:00-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T01:25\",\"n\":\"Earlier overnight arrival via Taipei\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO at noon and arrives in Bangkok at 1:25 a.m. on January 17, via Taipei, with one stop and 22h 25m elapsed. This Aeroplan economy award requires 65,000 points plus CAD 116.50 in taxes, with 1 seat reported. Compared with the Hong Kong award, it arrives 9h 10m earlier, which may suit you if reaching Bangkok overnight matters; you give up the Hong Kong option’s 2h 5m shorter elapsed journey and lower reported taxes (CAD 107.40). The Taipei connection is 4h 30m. Leg-by-leg cabin details and quote scope are unknown.\"}]},{\"start\":5,\"end\":6,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J20@2027-01-15T17:15-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T06:30\",\"n\":\"More reported seats; earlier morning arrival\",\"v\":\"Departs SFO at 5:15 p.m. and arrives in Bangkok at 6:30 a.m. on January 17, via Vancouver, with one stop and 22h 15m elapsed. The Aeroplan economy award requires 92,144 points plus CAD 43.90 in taxes, and 9 seats are reported. Compared with the Hong Kong award, it arrives 4h 5m earlier and reports more seats and lower taxes; choose it if those reported differences matter more than the higher points requirement (92,144 versus 65,000). Its elapsed journey is 1h 55m longer. The Vancouver connection is 3h 37m; leg-by-leg cabin details and quote scope are unknown.\"}]},{\"start\":7,\"end\":8,\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"The other Taipei award departs 15 minutes later than the Hong Kong option, but arrives 6h 15m later and takes 6 hours longer overall. It reports the same 65,000-point requirement and one seat, but higher taxes (CAD 116.50 versus CAD 107.40). The slightly later departure may fit your schedule; in exchange, you arrive later and spend more time traveling, with no reported seat-count advantage.\"}]}]}"
